================================================================================
  slftp -- cbftp offload
================================================================================

  slftp brain + cbftp FTP engine
  Requires the paid version of cbftp ;)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This branch offloads all FTP operations to cbftp. slftp becomes the
"brain" -- handling IRC announces, rule evaluation, routing decisions and
race orchestration -- while cbftp executes the actual transfers.

A REST API (mORMot2) and React-based Web UI remain included for monitoring,
configuration, and operational control.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARCHITECTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    +-------------+     IRC announces      +-------------+
    |   IRC       | <--------------------> |   slftp     |
    |  networks   |                        |  (brain)    |
    +-------------+                        |             |
                                           |  +-------+  |
                                           |  | Rules |  |
                                           |  | Engine|  |
                                           |  +---+---|  |
                                           |      |      |
                                           |  +---v---+  |     UDP 5696    +-------------+
                                           |  | Race  |  | --------------> |   cbftp     |
                                           |  |Control|  |   Spread Jobs   |             |
                                           |  +---+---|  |                 |  FTP Engine |
                                           |      |      |                 |  Transfers  |
                                           |  +---v---+  | <-------------- |  Connections|
                                           |  | REST  |  |   UDP 5697      +-------------+
                                           |  | API   |  |   Events
                                           |  |(mORMot)| |
                                           |  +---+---|  |
                                           |      |      |
                                           |  +---v---+  |
                                           |  |Web UI |  |
                                           |  |(React)| |
                                           |  +-------+  |
                                           +-------------+

Communication Flow:

  1. IRC -> slftp     Announce parsing, rule evaluation, KB updates
  2. slftp -> cbftp   Spread jobs via REST API (POST /spreadjobs) or UDP
  3. cbftp -> slftp   Race events via UDP push:
                      race_started, race_progress, race_completed,
                      race_done, speed_sample, nfo_available, site_status
  4. Web UI -> slftp  Dashboard, stats, file browser, cbftp job monitor
  5. Web UI -> cbftp  Live site status, transfer jobs, routes (proxied)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KEY DIFFERENCES FROM NATIVE slftp
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Area                    Native slftp               cbftp offload
  ----------------------  -------------------------  --------------------------
  FTP Engine              Native slftp               Delegated to cbftp
  Site Slots              Active FTP logins          Sites set to permdown
  Race Control            slftp manages transfers    slftp sends spread jobs
  Event Model             Internal task queue        UDP event push from cbftp
  Stats / Ranks           Internal transfers         cbftp speed_sample events
  NFO Download            Native FTP tasks           cbftp REST (GET /file)
  Dirlist (genre/WebUI)   Native FTP LIST            cbftp REST (GET /path)
  Raw Commands            Native FTP socket          Proxied via cbftp REST
  Race Stats IRC          Native output              From cbftp events
  SFV Verification        Native tasks               Disabled (cbftp handles)
  Web UI File Browser     slftp BrowserService       cbftp /path API
  Web UI cbftp Tab        Not present                Jobs, sites, routes

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIGURATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Enable cbftp mode in slftp.ini:

  [UDPConfig]
  EnableUDP=1
  IP=127.0.0.1
  Port=5696
  ApiPort=55477
  Password=your_cbftp_api_password
  EventPushBindIP=127.0.0.1
  EventPushPort=5697
  EncryptUDP=1

In cbftp, configure the UDP push target in the cbftp Main Screen
(Global Options -> UDP push target). Set IP and port to match
slftp's EventPushBindIP / EventPushPort.

Site Setup:

  slftp displays site up/down status directly from cbftp via:
    - UDP site_status events (pushed by cbftp)
    - Live REST API polling (cbftp sites table in Web UI)

  Sites can be kept active in slftp for BNC management, or set to
  permdown to conserve resources:

    !setpermdown * 1

  Rules always evaluate regardless of permdown status when UDP is
  enabled. cbftp handles all actual FTP connections and transfers.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT WORKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Core (unchanged):
  - IRC announce processing and precatcher
  - Rule evaluation (allow/block, section, affil, pretime)
  - API-based rules (tvgenres, imdbgenre, imdbrating, etc.)
  - Knowledge base and release tracking
  - Route calculation and speed-based routing

cbftp Integration:
  - Spread Jobs: POST /spreadjobs with section, release, target sites
  - UDP Events: race_started, race_progress, race_completed, race_done,
                speed_sample, nfo_available, site_status
  - Stats Processing: SpeedStatAdd, statsProcessRace, RanksProcess from events
  - NFO Download: GET /file via cbftp REST, genre extraction
  - Raw Commands: SITE INVITE, SITE RULES etc. proxied through cbftp
  - Dirlist: GET /path for MP3/MVID genre lookups and Web UI file browser
  - Auto-Invite: PermDown sites invited via cbftp REST
  - Site Status Sync: cbftp disabled status reflected in slftp
  - Completion Times: Millisecond-precision from cbftp TimeSpentSeconds
  - cbftp Latency Tracking: Detection-to-spread timing per release

IRC Output (cbftp event-driven):
  - [CBFTP]   Spread job announcement with target sites
  - [RACE]    Per-file transfer speed samples from cbftp
  - [STATS]   Race completion stats with site times and speeds

Web UI:
  - Dashboard: cbftp version/uptime, active races, transfer counters
  - Race Stats: Live and historical data from cbftp events
  - File Browser: Browses sites via cbftp /path API
  - cbftp Main Screen: Spread jobs (WORST/AVG/BEST, status, progress),
                       live sites table with 5s polling
  - Routes: Route matrix, speed/flag config, drag-and-drop site palette,
            bulk operations, affiliated targets
  - Active Tasks: Running races and queued transfers (live)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGES OR IS LIMITED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Feature                 Status   Notes
  ----------------------  -------  ------------------------------------------
  mp3genre rule           Works    Via TPazoGenreDirlistTask + cbftp GetPath
  nfogenre rule           Works    Via cetNfoAvailable event + cbftp GetFile
  mvidgenre rule          Works    Via TPazoMVIDTask + cbftp GetPath/GetFile
  SFV verification        Disabled cbftp handles file integrity
  Native race stats       Replaced By cbftp event-driven [STATS] / [RACE]
  Native FTP racing       Disabled Tuzelj exits immediately with UDP
  Normal race dirlist     Skipped  Not needed; cbftp handles dirlisting

Genre / NFO Details:

  The NFO download is now conditional: slftp only fetches NFOs when
  active rules actually require them (mp3genre or nfogenre). This is
  determined dynamically via RulesNeedNfo() rather than a fixed config.

  mp3genre:
    - Task: TPazoGenreDirlistTask is created in UDP mode
    - Fetches dirlist via cbftp REST GetPath()
    - Extracts genre from tags in the dirlist output

  nfogenre:
    - Native TPazoGenreNfoTask is NOT created in UDP mode
    - Instead: cbftp sends nfo_available UDP event when NFO is ready
    - slftp fetches the NFO via cbftp REST GetFile() and extracts genre

  mvidgenre:
    - Task: TPazoMVIDTask is created in UDP mode
    - Fetches dirlist via cbftp REST GetPath()
    - Downloads SFV + NFO via cbftp REST GetFile()
    - Parses genre and video region from NFO content

Code State:
  This branch is functionally complete but still contains significant
  legacy code from the native FTP engine (taskrace, tuzelj, native
  dirlist tasks, SFV verification, etc.) that is no longer executed
  in cbftp mode. A full cleanup of dead code paths is planned but
  not yet complete.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REST API ENDPOINTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

cbftp Proxy (via slftp API):

  GET  /api/cbftp/sites                 List all cbftp sites
  GET  /api/cbftp/sites/:name           Site details + live stats
  GET  /api/cbftp/sections              List sections
  GET  /api/cbftp/spreadjobs            List spread jobs
  GET  /api/cbftp/spreadjobs/:name      Spread job details
  GET  /api/cbftp/transferjobs          List transfer jobs
  POST /api/cbftp/raw                   Send raw FTP command
  GET  /api/cbftp/info                  cbftp version & uptime
  GET  /api/cbftp/path?site=X&path=Y    Directory listing

slftp Native API:

  GET /api/stats/races                  Race statistics
  GET /api/tasks/active                 Active tasks (races + transfers)
  GET /api/cbftp/enabled                Returns {"enabled":true/false}
  GET /api/cbftp/main                   Cached cbftp jobs + sites
